      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T23:17:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both checks are actually identical! `SubmitRequirementResult.Status` has 7 enum values total: four of them (`SATISFIED`, `OVERRIDDEN`, `NOT_APPLICABLE`, `FORCED`) return `true` for `fulfilled()`, while the remaining three (`UNSATISFIED`, `ERROR`, `TIMEOUT`) return `false`.\n\nTherefore, checking `UNSATISFIED || ERROR || TIMEOUT` is the exact negation of `sr.fulfilled()`.\n\nThat said, using two different styles for the same condition is confusing. I\u0027ve updated `UNMET_REQUIREMENT_FIELD` to use `!sr.fulfilled()` so both fields use consistent logic.",
      "parentUuid": "7ff465ef_376d7284",
      "revId": "527652179a64b4cec32c6641cfa287de33f53a76",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
